      "source": "base word of “rüzgârlı” (A2-5A, Turkishle)",
      "notes": "The â marks a palatalised g: [ɟ], not the velar [ɡ]. Convention: IPA, with ˈ before the stressed syllable, ː for length, [æ] vs [e] for the two e qualities, [c]/[ɟ] for palatalised k/g, and [l] vs [ɫ] for clear and dark l. Transcribed by hand — TDK supplies length, stress and a prose note on l, but not the vowel allophony or the k/g palatalisation, so this cannot be generated.",
